From: LR-Vensuki <260785366+LR-Vensuki@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 17:17:40 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] xhttp client: shape requests like newer Xray

Newer Xray servers can expect packet-up data in numbered headers
(X-Data-N) or cookies (x_data_N) instead of the body, GET uploads, the
session id and sequence number in a header, cookie or query, and the
padding under its own key and placement. Fronts that refuse request bodies
answer a body with 413, and a server looking elsewhere for the ids answers
400.

New client options, all defaulting to the current behaviour:
uplink_http_method, uplink_data_placement, uplink_data_key,
uplink_chunk_size, session_placement/session_key, seq_placement/seq_key,
x_padding_obfs_mode, x_padding_placement, x_padding_key, x_padding_header.
The path keeps its trailing slash only when an id rides in it, and the
padding URL is the path before the ids, as in Xray. Checked against an
Xray server for every placement.
